engineering|technical-design|NOUN|designing and building using technical knowledge|The work or study of using scientific and practical knowledge to design, build, and improve structures or machines.|kỹ thuật; ngành kỹ thuật|She studies engineering and hopes to design safer bridges.|Cô ấy học ngành kỹ thuật và mong thiết kế những cây cầu an toàn hơn.|Uncountable for the field; an engineering project names an application, not an engineering.|0
inadvertent|unintentional|ADJECTIVE|done without intending it|Happening or being done without intention, often because something was not noticed.|vô ý; không cố ý|An inadvertent change to the address sent the parcel to another street.|Một thay đổi vô ý ở địa chỉ khiến bưu kiện được gửi sang đường khác.|Usually before a noun such as error or omission; does not itself mean harmless.|-
nod|head-signal|VERB|move the head as a signal|To move your head briefly down and up, often to show agreement or recognition.|gật đầu|She nodded to show that she had understood the instructions.|Cô ấy gật đầu để cho biết mình đã hiểu hướng dẫn.|Usually intransitive; nod to someone identifies a recipient, and nod one's head uses an object.|0
nod|sleepy-movement|VERB|let the head drop when sleepy|To let your head drop briefly because you are sleepy.|gật gù vì buồn ngủ|The passenger began to nod as the bus moved through the quiet streets.|Hành khách bắt đầu gật gù vì buồn ngủ khi xe buýt đi qua những con phố yên tĩnh.|Intransitive; nod off means begin to fall asleep and is a related phrasal construction.|1
throne|royal-seat|NOUN|ceremonial seat of a ruler|A special chair used by a king, queen, or other ruler on formal occasions.|ngai; ngai vàng|The carved throne stood at the far end of the hall.|Chiếc ngai chạm khắc đặt ở cuối phía bên kia của đại sảnh.|Countable for the chair; the throne can also refer to royal authority in another use.|-
width|side-distance|NOUN|measurement across something|The measurement of something from one side to the other.|chiều rộng; bề ngang|Measure the width of the doorway before moving the desk.|Đo chiều rộng cửa ra vào trước khi chuyển chiếc bàn.|Usually the width of something; a width of plus a measurement states its size.|0
